WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.970
<i>In this game, the only 
thing used is the body.</i>

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.470
<i>Working together with your teammates,</i>

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:11.940
<i>you capture the "raider" 
invading your territory.</i>

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.510
<i>Dragging them down and forcing 
them out leads to victory.</i>

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:19.530
<i>If you had to describe the way it looks, 
it might be a "running combat sport."</i>

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.350
<i>The name of this game is...</i>

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:22.990
<i>kabaddi!</i>

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.550
What Is
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKabaddi?

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.550
<i>I took entering high school as my opportunity</i>

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.950
<i>to live a life as far away 
from sports as possible.</i>

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.560
<b>Noukin High School, First-year
Yoigoshi Tatsuya</b>

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.560
<i>I hate all sports.</i>

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:10.770
<i>Coaches that get spitting mad 
at the slightest mistakes...</i>

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.570
<b>Under 15
Yoigoshi the Unstoppable
Rising Youth Kicker</b>

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:14.220
<i>The sports media that get rattled by a 
middle schooler's choice of schools...</i>

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.000
Always hogging all the attention.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.430
He needs to quit acting so 
full of himself. I could...

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.070
<i>Teammates wallowing in jealousy 
and malicious gossip, all of it...</i>

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.230
That's gotta be it.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.080
<i>I hate all of it.</i>

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.100
Yoigoshi! I know you're in there! Come out!

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.040
Come on! Join the team, even 
just as a provisional member!

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:34.960
Yoigoshi!

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.510
Sports are stupid.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:38.170
Go away!

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.180
You're just a first-year kid. What makes you 
think you can talk to us like that—

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.540
It's fine! He can talk down 
to us or whatever he wants!

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.360
Just, please, let's play soccer together—

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.810
"Together"?

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:55.020
I hate hanging around sportsmen.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.450
Th-That was scary...

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.170
He's not right in the head.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.710
<i>I know a much smarter, 
much cooler way to communicate.</i>

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.090
<i>That's right.</i>

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.340
<i>Micomico Livestreaming!</i>

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:18.170
<b>Micomico Douga</b>

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.810
<i>Micomico Douga!</i>

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:19.920
Now, then...

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.930
No livestreams scheduled.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.930
<b>New Community Members</b>

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.930
<b>New Members (6 people)</b>

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.930
The community membership is increasing!

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.110
It's moving in a pretty good direction.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.310
A troll, huh? Better report it.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:36.200
A world where I can erase those 
I don't like with a single finger.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.520
This is the best!

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:39.440
Now, it is time.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.630
Let's begin.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.610
The livestream of the Night's End!

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.740
We're just chatting today. 
Ask me whatever questions you want.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:54.380
Comment

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:54.380
Comment

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:54.380
Hey, there

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:54.380
He's here

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:54.380
Night's End, you're

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.880
<i>Night's End, you're a student, right?</i>

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:53.930
Yes. I am a student, but I do not 
wish to talk about my private life.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:58.880
<i>I want to keep my online and real lives 
separate. It'd be a pain otherwise.</i>

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:07.510
Comment

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:07.510
Comment

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:07.510
Hey, there

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:07.510
He's here

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:07.510
Night's End, you're

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:07.510
What a shame. Why

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:02.210
<i>What a shame. Why don't you 
join a club or something?</i>

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:07.510
You got invited right?

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.530
<i>You got invited right? To the soccer team.</i>

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:07.510
You might get invited again.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.700
<i>You might get invited again.</i>

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.660
I-I-Invitation?

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:11.020
What's going on here?

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.430
<i>Is this someone I know?</i>

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.130
<i>Was I naïve in thinking a mask would 
be enough to hide my identity?</i>

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.280
<i>Who is that, in this moment of crisis?</i>

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.850
<i>Those soccer players from earlier?</i>

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:27.410
'Sup?!

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.240
Is there a guy named "Yoigoshi" here?

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:32.750
Who are you?

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:37.010
Oh, are you alone? I thought 
I heard you talking to someone...

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.670
O-Oh, yeah...

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.270
I was on the phone.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.430
More importantly, what did you want?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.430
Oh! So, you're Yoigoshi, huh?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:51.870
Sir!

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:57.940
<b>Noukin High School
Azemichi Soma</b>

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.670
I'm first-year Azemichi Soma!

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:57.940
I came to invite you to 
join the kabaddi team!

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.290
K-Kabaddi?

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:03.520
<i>I've know the name, but I didn't 
know we had a team here.</i>

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.680
<i>It's got nothing to do with me, though.</i>

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.420
It takes some guts for a first-year 
to invite me into a club,

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:12.170
but go away.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.460
I have no intention of playing 
sports in high school.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:17.460
J-Just hold on a sec!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.290
"Go bring us that Yoigoshi 
who's famous for soccer,"

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.390
that's what my senpai asked me to do.

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:24.970
Hey! What're you doing? Let go!

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.210
I'm begging you!

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.990
Just provisionally, no, even if 
you just come as an observer!

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.470
Let go of me!

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.370
<i>What? I can't move him!</i>

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.980
<i>That's not possible! 
He's so much smaller than I am!</i>

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:43.640
How's that? Learned your lesson?

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.490
Just come and watch...

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:50.690
<i>He's not gonna leave, huh?</i>

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.630
<i>This is different from the 
other invites I've received.</i>

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:54.170
<i>This one's trouble.</i>

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.590
<i>As long as he's here, 
I can't restart my livestream.</i>

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.500
<i>I've got no choice. I don't want to, but...</i>

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.690
I just need to go watch?

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.670
Huh? Oh. Yeah, probably.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:05.750
Okay. I'll get ready to go.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:07.720
Really? All right!

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.750
<i>If I'm going to sever this relationship,</i>

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.040
<i>instead of trying with 
this stubborn errand boy,</i>

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:15.220
<i>it seems like it would be faster to 
talk to these upperclassmen of his.</i>

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.230
<b>Noukin High School</b>

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:21.110
Yoigoshi, thanks for being 
so quick to understand.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.670
<i>I'm not interested in joining 
the team, but thinking about it,</i>

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.300
<i>kabaddi will probably make 
a good topic for a chat.</i>

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.290
<i>I am the very epitome of livestream hosts.</i>

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.590
Oh, yeah. Are you sure you 
didn't want to change clothes?

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:33.830
Huh? Oh, yes. I'm only 
planning to watch, after all.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.450
Oh, come on. It'd be better if you tried it.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:37.990
Why would I do that?

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:39.270
Chanting "kabaddi" while you run.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:41.850
There are a lot of gags about 
that ridiculous sport, aren't there?

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.720
It's not ridiculous!

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:49.270
Kabaddi is a sport unlike any other! 
A team sport with no equipment!

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:53.180
You fight using just your and your 
teammates bodies. It's an intense sport!

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.860
<i>Why's he getting all worked up? 
It's so suffocating.</i>

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:59.390
<i>But a team sport with no equipment, huh?</i>

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.810
<i>I've never heard of that before.</i>

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:03.360
Senpai! Yoigoshi's here!

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:04.310
Gymnasium 1

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.540
<i>They're using the old gym?</i>

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.380
<i>Well, it is just a colorful 
little sport, after all.</i>

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:20.580
Hey! It's Yoigoshi!

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:24.040
<i>What was that? 
This is the kabaddi team, right?</i>

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:33.430
<b>Kabaddi Team Second-year
Misumi Kyohei</b>

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:33.430
<b>Kabaddi Team Second-year
Date Shinji</b>

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:27.790
He's tall. About 185 centimeters?

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.590
Wow. You're even cooler than your 
soccer photos make you look.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:33.430
<i>Do guys with builds like that play it?</i>

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.570
He doesn't have much muscle. 
About 75 kilos, maybe?

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:37.310
Hey!

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:38.890
Well, he did play soccer.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:41.140
His kicking was amazing!

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.450
Stay away from me, you musclebound morons!

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:47.010
Aw, come on. Let's be friends.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.140
We're gonna be on this team together, right?

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:51.690
No! I'm not here because I want to be—

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:51.690
Hey!

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:53.660
It's rude to go in so suddenly, guys.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:55.870
Sorry about that, Yoigoshi-kun.

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:59.210
Everyone's just excited 
about meeting someone famous.

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:02.710
<b>Kabaddi Team Third-year
Iura Kei</b>

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:03.020
I'm the kabaddi team's vice-captain, Iura. 
Nice to meet you.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.070
Vice-captain?

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:07.580
Sorry to send a first-year 
after you like that.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.750
It should have been me,

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.170
but since the captain's hospitalized, 
I've been so busy.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:15.100
<i>So it was the vice-captain 
who sent baldy after me?</i>

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.350
<i>But that's a relief.</i>

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:19.720
<i>He seems the most likely to listen 
to reason here. A nice type of guy.</i>

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:24.730
<b>Heave-ho</b>

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:24.730
<b>Heave-ho</b>

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:23.080
<i>Because I'd really hate getting forced 
to participate in practice or something.</i>

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.730
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:28.230
Allow me to introduce you. 
Those two are second-years—

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.940
I don't need introductions. 
I need to talk to you.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.740
What's wrong? That's a scary expression.

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:36.270
I was pretty much dragged here against 
my will. I'm not joining the team!

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:39.330
Don't say that. Won't you wait and 
make a decision after you've tried it?

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.630
If you're short on members, you 
can try someone else, can't you?

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:46.250
Someone else, huh? 
Well, we are short on members, but...

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.420
It's you the kabaddi team wants, Yoigoshi.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.710
<b>"Yoigoshi the Unstoppable" Unprecedented Forward, Plays Dirty</b>

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.710
"Yoigoshi the Unstoppable."

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.570
Soccer's a sport with a lot of contact, 
and he's never been taken down.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.990
<b>"Yoigoshi the Unstoppable"</b>

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:56.930
We've been looking for someone who 
specializes in that kind of running.

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.900
I just hated other people 
touching me, that's all.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.240
More importantly, I'm so busy, 
I can't join a team.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:07.440
<b>Night's End</b>

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:07.440
<i>I have to livestream on a regular 
schedule or my fans will leave me.</i>

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.450
So, livestreaming keeps you that busy?

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:11.230
Yeah.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:13.940
What?!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.270
<i>This guy... He knows?</i>

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:21.810
I just love Yoigo—Night's End's 
livestreams so much, I record them!

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:24.870
I wish everyone in the school could see them!

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.140
I'm all ready to send it to everyone, see?

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.550
You evil... Is this a threat?

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:34.270
Far from it! As a fan, I simply 
want to spread the word!

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:37.310
More importantly, I'll say this again...

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:40.890
Won't you try it out, just for today?

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:44.490
What're you guys talking about, 
bringing out your computer like that?

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:46.060
Well, the thing is...

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:48.900
Wait! All right! If it's just for today!

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.900
<i>He was not a nice type of guy!</i>

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:58.690
Since we have a beginner,
 we'll start with the basics.

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:00.020
Sir!

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.510
It's rough enough that they 
need to lay down these mats?

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:05.410
And they seem to have a scoreboard up.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.480
But what kind of sport is kabaddi anyway?

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:11.040
It's an intense sport!

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.490
A cool sport!

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:14.310
Where muscles clash!

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:16.430
I don't get it, and quit crowding me!

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:20.710
Put simply, kabaddi is like tag.

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:24.430
It's a sport where two teams 
try to tag each other on the court.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.540
Like tag?

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:29.630
Okay, guys. Let's try a little match.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:30.440
Sir!

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.200
I'll be attacking!

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:41.860
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi,

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:46.190
kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:50.210
In kabaddi, you have raiders and defenders.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.770
Who's raiding and who's defending 
is clearly defined through turns.

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.900
If you think of it like tag, 
the raider is "it."

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.710
He goes alone to try to tag the opponents.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.220
<b>Raider (It)
Azemichi Soma</b>

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.220
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.720
<b>Defense (Runners)
Second-years</b>

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.720
Still got a ways to go!

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:12.730
<b>Azemichi's Territory</b>

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:12.730
<b>Second-years' Territory</b>

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.140
The defense has multiple players

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.050
and they try to run from the 
raider without getting tagged.

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:10.310
They can run anywhere within 
their half of the court.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.730
The territories are defined by the mid-line.

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:15.620
How are they supposed to keep 
running in that tiny space?

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:17.780
That is why there are restrictions, of course.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:21.740
The raider can only cross the 
mid-line and go after opponents

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:25.110
for the amount of time they can say 
"kabaddi" without taking a breath.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:28.250
<i>So that's why they're always 
saying "kabaddi, kabaddi."</i>

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:31.660
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:31.660
A tag counts anywhere on the body.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:32.940
Kabaddi!

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:36.250
The slightest graze against the clothes, 
or even a single hair, counts as a tag.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.300
A single hair?

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.810
So, the tags are what gets you points?

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:43.750
Well... close.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:45.990
After contact is made, you get 
what's called the "struggle."

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:49.740
It's the state right before you get points, 
when you have them in your hand.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:50.980
Struggle?

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:56.230
The raider only gets the points once
 he returns to his own territory.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:59.950
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:03.530
We're in the struggle.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.930
Come on, now.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:07.580
Kabaddi! Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:09.650
"Return to his territory"? 
Can't he just go back?

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:10.270
Kabaddi! Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:13.890
Kabaddi... I can't make it back...

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:19.800
<b>Raid Failed</b>

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:15.700
That was close!

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:19.800
You... You just wanted to show Yoigoshi, 
and let yourself get tagged, didn't you?

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:23.840
If the defense can capture the raider,

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:26.960
preventing him from returning, 
then they get a point.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:29.880
Alternating this attack and defense 
pattern gives you kabaddi.

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:31.460
That's a simplistic explanation, anyway.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:34.260
Why don't you give it a try?

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:35.440
That?

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:37.190
You'll be fine!

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:41.190
Well then, I'll be the raider, 
just to test things out.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:44.660
No catching—that is, no tackling.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.980
We'll just be playing a simple 
game of tag within the court.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.200
You two, use your heads and run away, okay?

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:52.200
Yes, sir!

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:56.350
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:59.140
<i>"Use your heads and run away"?</i>

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:00.960
<i>Who needs brains in a game of tag?</i>

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:02.510
<i>This way's no good!</i>

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.280
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:11.260
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.410
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.090
Right! With the two of you, 
that's two points.

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:21.040
You're too fast, Iura-senpai.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:23.230
Now, the two of you try it.

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:25.400
I'll watch from the outside and collect data.

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:28.810
And, one thing...

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:32.160
The way you ran just now was odd.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.180
You changed direction suddenly, didn't you?

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:35.510
Why?

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:38.420
Huh? That's obvious, isn't it?

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:42.420
You were trying to herd me and baldy 
in the same direction, weren't you?

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:47.300
We both ended up getting tagged, 
so it didn't end up mattering, but—

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.470
Kabaddi!

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:51.050
You should never let your 
guard down, Yoigoshi!

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:52.510
Don't underestimate kabaddi!

00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:58.240
Kabaddi...

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:01.900
It is, indeed, an idiotic 
sport played by idiots.

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:03.530
However...

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:07.030
getting dissed by idiots grinds my gears!

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:10.790
What's this?

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:12.990
I don't hear you saying "kabaddi"!

00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:17.130
K-kabaddi... Kabaddi...

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.890
He seems embarrassed to do the chant.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:21.920
But he's an interesting guy. He saw 
what I was trying for right away.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:24.790
Kabaddi... kabaddi... kabaddi...

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:25.790
I thought he only had height 
and good reflexes,

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.880
but he's got good judgment and he's proud.

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.550
<b>Raider
Attacker</b>

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.320
He's a raider-type.

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:33.340
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:36.980
He's the opposite type to 
the little guy, Azemichi.

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:39.770
He's more suited to being an anti.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:41.440
<b>Anti
Defense</b>

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:44.690
What's wrong? I'm a rookie here, you know.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:48.970
Is this a plan to let me 
win to make me feel good?

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:51.180
If this were just tag, 
he'd be in a bad position.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:52.450
Well...

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.410
I don't know about that...

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:59.090
Don't you think the people who are 
good at raiding are a little twisted?

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:00.460
<b>Raider-type</b>

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:02.460
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:08.200
This kabaddi or whatever 
isn't anything special.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:10.470
You can't touch me at all.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.740
Blast it! I'm not done yet!

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:16.930
It's already eight. It's about time I...

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.770
Gather up! That's the end of practice.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:20.940
Finally.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.270
Sorry for threatening you.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:28.280
<b>Deleted</b>

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:26.400
All the recordings and the messages. See?

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.280
You did that pretty easily.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.910
And there's a little thank you.

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:30.860
A "thank you"?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.450
Micomi
Community

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.450
<b>Night's End-san's Community</b>

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.630
My community page?

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:38.950
New Community Members

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:38.950
New Members (107 people)

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:38.950
Glasses Girl

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:38.950
Hiro

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:38.950
Guest

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:36.460
Wh-What is all this?

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.950
My membership has increased 
by over a hundred people?

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:43.020
The thing is, I know a lot of different 
people on the net, you see.

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:44.600
I promoted you a bit.

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:49.560
I've lost count of how many godly 
livecasters I've created this way.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:53.470
They're all dummy accounts, but people 
do gather where there are people, right?

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.410
<i>"Godly livecasters"?</i>

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:59.330
If you joined the team, I could increase 
you membership by several thousand...

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.090
But, joining the team is a little—

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.350
You feel the need to think when 
things happen suddenly, right?

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.280
Then, how about a game?

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:09.220
One-on-one kabaddi with Azemichi. 
If you lose, you join the team,

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:11.680
but if you win, I'll increase 
your community memberships.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.990
And, of course, you won't 
have to join the team.

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:16.100
Compete against him?

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:18.490
In practice, he couldn't even touch me.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:23.130
But this time, you'll be playing 
closer to the official rules.

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:24.790
The defenders are allowed to tackle.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:29.460
If the raider is taken down in the defense's 
territory, the defense gets a point.

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:30.830
What do you think?

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.330
<i>So, takedowns are possible.</i>

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:36.340
<i>Even up against all the players on the 
field in soccer, no one took me down.</i>

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:38.800
<i>And in terms of speed, I have this guy beat.</i>

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:41.110
<i>This is a contest I'm certain to win.</i>

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:44.190
Sounds like fun. I'll take that challenge.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:50.690
Azemichi

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:50.690
Yoigoshi

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:48.960
Playing to two points!

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:50.690
Yoigoshi on offense. Begin!

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.700
I'm not losing again! Bring it on, Yoigo—

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:56.700
<i>H-He's super-focused.</i>

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.320
<i>Godly livestreamer.</i>

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:02.600
<i>Just two points, and I have 
a chance at that throne.</i>

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:04.710
Kabaddi. Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:04.710
<i>I cannot let this opportunity pass me by.</i>

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:06.470
Kabaddi.

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:07.710
He doesn't seem embarrassed anymore.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.710
It just shows how desperate 
he must be feeling.

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:12.090
But that was a nice move there.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.030
Getting him to let down 
his guard by playing tag.

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:15.780
Then, in a serious match with 
joining the team on the line,

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.450
setting him up against that Azemichi?

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:19.510
I'm sure he'll notice along the way.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.720
Kabaddi...

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.810
is a combat sport.

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:25.940
Kabaddi!

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:25.940
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:27.130
Huh?

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:30.120
Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:34.190
Azemichi

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:34.190
Yoigoshi

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:34.190
True, this does seem like the kind 
of thing that gets a point, but...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.810
All right! That's one point!

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:38.060
Don't give me, "all right"!

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:39.910
Punching's against the rules!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.370
A touch is a touch!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:43.200
Just how desperate are you?!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.680
Besides, I didn't know that!

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:47.930
It's fine. He can have the point.

00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:51.060
With his hand in a fist, 
his reach was shorter.

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:52.710
It's my fault for letting my guard down.

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:54.710
Reach?

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.150
<i>I see.</i>

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:59.470
<i>He's right. I shouldn't make 
a fist if I don't need to.</i>

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.430
<b>Raider Azemichi</b>

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.430
<b>Azemichi</b>

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.430
<b>Yoigoshi</b>

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:02.430
Next, Azemichi will be on offense.

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:07.390
<i>It's similar to tag, but in this game, 
kabaddi, played on this small court...</i>

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.880
<i>reach is everything!</i>

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:11.190
<i>Of course, increasing the area in 
which you can tag is a given,</i>

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.780
<i>but even if you get tackled by the defense,</i>

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:14.230
<b>Safe
Area</b>

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:14.230
<i>you can fall onto your own territory.</i>

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:19.150
<i>Which means that as long as I don't get 
taken down deep in the court, I'll be fine!</i>

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:19.590
Kabaddi! Kabaddi! Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.770
<i>But it's different for the shrimp.</i>

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:25.010
<i>If I tackle him at this distance,
 he can't get back!</i>

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:25.880
Kabaddi?

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:28.250
He went for a tackle!

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:30.680
It's over! This is my second point!

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:30.950
Kabaddi.

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:33.360
Ka...bad...di!

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:37.310
<i>H-He's not going down?!</i>

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:40.640
Kabaddi!

00:18:41.110 --> 00:18:43.760
Thanks for coming in to make 
contact yourself. That helped.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:47.160
Trying to tag you is crazy hard.

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:50.020
<i>He let me catch him on purpose?!</i>

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.520
Azemichi

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.520
Yoigoshi

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:53.520
Azemichi, raid successful! One point!

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:55.970
You were tricked by his size, right?

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:57.530
He surprises everyone.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:01.530
Azemichi's from a potter's family 
high up in the mountains.

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:05.540
According to him, his everyday life 
was like constant weight training.

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.660
<i>His everyday life was all weight training?</i>

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:10.540
One more point! Take him down, Azemichi!

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.420
Sir!

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.770
<i>I should have stuck to running.</i>

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:15.590
<b>Raider Yoigoshi</b>

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:15.590
<b>Azemichi</b>

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:15.590
<b>Yoigoshi</b>

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:15.590
<i>But now, I'm the raider.</i>

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:19.100
Kabaddi. Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:19.110
<i>When attacking, reach and 
speed determine everything.</i>

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:22.840
Kabaddi. Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.840
Now, what will you do, Yoigoshi?

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:26.330
Kabaddi. Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:29.690
Kabaddi. Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:30.010
He seems to have figured out at what 
distance he's guaranteed to make it back.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:32.560
That's a surprise. It's hard to do that.

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:34.690
Kabaddi. Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:37.770
<i>To win, you have to get 
close to your opponent.</i>

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:40.700
Kabaddi. Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:40.700
<i>But if you get close, the risk 
of being caught increases.</i>

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:45.600
<i>In most contact sports, 
you want to evade your opponents,</i>

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:46.700
<i>but in kabaddi...</i>

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:50.710
Kabaddi. Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:49.300
<i>to win, what you want is to face 
off against your opponents,</i>

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:50.710
<i>just like in combat sports!</i>

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:55.710
Azemichi! You're too focused!

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:04.140
<i>And, because it's so similar to combat sports, 
it makes a certain thing necessary.</i>

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.290
<i>A ranking system.</i>

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:10.790
<i>That's how big a handicap 
height and weight can become!</i>

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.200
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:16.820
<i>Now, all I need to do is take one step back.</i>

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:18.380
<i>This is farewell!</i>

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:20.210
<i>When I become a godly livecaster,</i>

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:23.240
<i>I'll tell people that kabaddi 
isn't just a sport for gags.</i>

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.330
Kabaddi—

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:31.250
Being tall means you more area to grab!

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.250
Kabaddi?

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:37.040
When I dragged you here...

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:39.750
I felt sort of bad about it.

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:41.540
But now I'm glad.

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:42.760
Kabaddi...

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.930
Yoigoshi, while we've been competing...

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:48.260
your face has said that you're having fun!

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:51.530
<i>Having fun? Playing kabaddi?</i>

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:53.260
<i>That's not possible—</i>

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:56.390
<i>I can do this! It's just one step!</i>

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:56.390
Kabaddi...

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:57.660
Kabaddi...

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:59.070
<i>If I reach, I can make it!</i>

00:20:57.660 --> 00:21:00.780
Kabaddi... Kabaddi...

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.780
<i>Just a few centimeters!</i>

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:03.040
<i>Make it... Make it...</i>

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:03.960
Kabaddi!

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:04.920
<i>Make it!</i>

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:09.030
Yoigoshi, starting now, we're teammates!

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:11.170
I'm counting on you!

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:19.540
Azemichi

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:19.540
Yoigoshi

00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:16.980
Yoigoshi, raid failed.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:19.540
One point to Azemichi on defense.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:21.300
End of match!

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:23.400
With 2 to 1, Azemichi wins!

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:31.420
Year 1, Class 1, Azemichi Soma!

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:34.350
I have played kabaddi for one month. 
The thing I love most is kabaddi!

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:38.110
Second-year, Misumi Kyohei.

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:40.070
I've been playing kabaddi for 
one year and one month.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.690
What I love is cool stuff!

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:43.560
Same year, Date Shinji!

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:45.190
I've played kabaddi for six months!

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:47.200
What I love is muscles!

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:48.840
Don't introduce yourselves...

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:54.220
Third-year, Iura Kei.

00:21:54.220 --> 00:21:55.870
I've been playing kabaddi for six years.

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:58.920
What I love is the internet. What I hate...

00:21:59.310 --> 00:22:01.710
is people who don't keep their promises.

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:06.840
<b>Club Registration</b>

00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:06.010
Welcome to the kabaddi team!

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:10.340
<i>And thus I was dragged into the kabaddi team.</i>

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:14.930
<i>No matter how much I hate sports 
and groups reeking of sweat,</i>

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:17.640
<i>there's no way to send a report 
or flag in regular life.</i>

00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:23.820
Captain (Cap)

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:26.820
<b>Meisei Hospital</b>

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:26.820
Hello, Kei?

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:30.840
Yeah. They said I'll probably 
be discharged next month.

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.270
<i>Did anyone else join?</i>

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:36.830
Yes, someone joined. Someone interesting.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"Men Who Connect"</b>

00:23:49.370 --> 00:23:52.610
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:50.990
Next time!

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:52.610
"Men Who Connect."

00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:53.260
Kabaddi!
